ld/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11bd8602-a2be-5ae4-8ba8-6a2ffe62757c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127043" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y=5-4t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ 5-4t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}t \\\\ -4t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,5,\\frac{1}{7})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da7c2733-20e6-5a35-8787-d2cda7011df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314768} {:answer/id #uuid "a44fe621-56df-5496-85e3-f4315c8a6fc5"