 substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-4+4t \\\\ y=-2+10t \\\\ z=4-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df6896fd-417d-5d7a-a828-28c46e947e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314837} {:answer/id #uuid "0252b975-5bf2-5414-8b2b-4ba7986107f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0252b975-5bf2-5414-8b2b-4ba7986107f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314838} :answer-field/id #uuid "08c0fe54-ddc5-55fb-a957-7a4c0f6885f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6488fa5e-3f35-5dec-9323-5a92facd38b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6488fa5e-3f35-5dec-9323-5a92facd38b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314840} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ce2553b-7bbe-5811-9554-53be6bba350c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39c8ef12-cb12-5036-895e-7cf2a1c19b74" :question/math-academy-id "q-236988" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(6,2,1)$ and $Q(4,10,2).$\n\n| $x=$ | $6-2t$ | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-1}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ 8t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6-2t \\\\ 2+8t \\\\ 1+t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6-2t \\\\ y=2+8t \\\\ z=1+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62a025e7-22f9-55a7-bbec-9097a8473a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314843} {:answer/id #uuid "1aace4d2-f6bb-5a1c-932a-7999444d7f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62a025e7-22f9-55a7-bbec-9097a8473a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314843} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac00e134-fb5e-53b9-991c-6c847a1416c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74e7409c-22e7-5d40-a6de-ccaadd3efcd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e7409c-22e7-5d40-a6de-ccaadd3efcd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314846} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3c61ccd-cd26-564a-99e4-21625f8441de" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8cbe2a7-0a06-5ac6-9b88-c4bca06e5838" :question/math-academy-id "q-236991" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(2,1,0)$ and $Q(3,2,-1).$\n\n| $x=$ | $2+t$ | $t\\in [$ {{field-1}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| $z=$ | $-t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+t \\\\ 1+t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=1+t \\\\ z=-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67cfb500-43a2-5211-8e9a-e3faebd7b5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314849} {:answer/id #uuid "0aeabd2b-6e76-586a-be05-d60c99344de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314850} {:answer/id #uuid "cf939b94-ee78-5c4e-84c4-ba0ecd81fc34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314851} {:answer/id #uuid "2b610f73-4981-5b93-8f36-423dd2860458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314852} {:answer/id #uuid "a66a1959-ab87-514d-9718-97791864a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a66a1959-ab87-514d-9718-97791864a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314853} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a9de36f-432b-5923-a955-e804f64b9e69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "276a7616-1504-50b7-889c-ca5f9580b20b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32785" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t-3 \\\\ y=7-9t \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3t-3 \\\\ 7-9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-3,7,-\\frac{1}{2})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5927f1da-2a1c-5173-a972-3c497b66ebcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314856} {:answer/id #uuid "c6247546-3221-5cff-b431-30772a0b0564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314857} {:answer/id #uuid "1b61d99c-b594-545a-bf37-e491e666a6f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314858} {:answer/id #uuid "5018e7cb-a5f1-5e8d-83e8-6c3e97ac72dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314859} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b32641-fde1-547e-b527-ad2504d05e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5927f1da-2a1c-5173-a972-3c497b66ebcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314856} :answer-field/id #uuid "a27f2749-0add-5621-9b27-c2e1f9e7e244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4aac5df8-4fac-5a42-a2e7-c1aa474eea31" :question/math-academy-id "q-70652" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-5t \\\\ y=2+t \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-5t \\\\ 2+t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5t \\\\ t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"}]}
